  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community-based management of human-elephant conflict in the North Kanara Landscape and transfer of Community-Based Conflict Management Technology to Forest Departments of other states in India</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to contribute to the conservation of wild Asian elephants in North Karnara, Karnataka, India by increasing the tolerance towards elephants via Community Based Conflict Management (CBCM), disseminate these techniques to other states of India, and influence wild elephant management policy at the national level. Specific activities will include: 1) capacity building in CBCM techniques, apiculture and bee hive fences; 2) training on local elephant-themed- handicrafts and elephant dung paper production; 3) educational film on elephant behavior and sociality produced and screened for local communities; 4) real-time internet-based monitoring of elephants in collaboration with the Karnataka Forest Department; and 5) transfer of CBCM techniques to Forest Departments of other state and influencing elephant management policies through workshops.</narrative>
  </description>
